{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-74412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int (1-2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}))\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fd0fe482f3cf2728f94910c390bc6c5e148a5e519583c93f66dbd58dbdbd73"} {"question" "q-74412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n1-2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (1-2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}))\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fd0fe482f3cf2728f94910c390bc6c5e148a5e519583c93f66dbd58dbdbd73"} {"question" "q-74412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96b3c950dde71577c2afac8d52c6a48bf7dc78542d6bc2bc6a74fa9e2099e0bc"} {"question" "q-74412" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fd0fe482f3cf2728f94910c390bc6c5e148a5e519583c93f66dbd58dbdbd73"} {"question" "q-74412" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fd0fe482f3cf2728f94910c390bc6c5e148a5e519583c93f66dbd58dbdbd73"} {"question" "q-74412" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fd0fe482f3cf2728f94910c390bc6c5e148a5e519583c93f66dbd58dbdbd73"} {"question" "q-114698" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int {cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fd0fe482f3cf2728f94910c390bc6c5e148a5e519583c93f66dbd58dbdbd73"} {"question" "q-114698" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1).\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fd0fe482f3cf2728f94910c390bc6c5e148a5e519583c93f66dbd58dbdbd73"} {"question" "q-114698" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96b3c950dde71577c2afac8d52c6a48bf7dc78542d6bc2bc6a74fa9e2099e0bc"} {"question" "q-114698" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fd0fe482f3cf2728f94910c390bc6c5e148a5e519583c93f66dbd58dbdbd73"} {"question" "q-114698" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2(x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+C"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x)+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{x}^{2}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fd0fe482f3cf2728f94910c390bc6c5e148a5e519583c93f66dbd58dbdbd73"} {"question" "q-114698" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x)+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fd0fe482f3cf2728f94910c390bc6c5e148a5e519583c93f66dbd58dbdbd73"} {"question" "q-348730" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/assets/fc3c0c02be98834937150e6bee5a52ac14246bc128b189d3c095269f788d97a9.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=-4{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+{x}^{2}+6,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fd0fe482f3cf2728f94910c390bc6c5e148a5e519583c93f66dbd58dbdbd73"} {"question" "q-348730" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(-4{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+{x}^{2}+6)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo calculate this integral, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rewrite the above formula as\n\n$$\n-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x=-4{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(-4{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+{x}^{2}+6)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+{x}^{2}+6)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+6x)\\,{|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{(\\pi /4)^{3}}{3}+6\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}]-[-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )+\\frac{(-\\pi /4)^{3}}{3}+6(-\\frac{\\pi }{4})] \\\\  & =(0+\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{192}+\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-(0-\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{192}-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{96}+3\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fd0fe482f3cf2728f94910c390bc6c5e148a5e519583c93f66dbd58dbdbd73"} {"question" "q-348730" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96b3c950dde71577c2afac8d52c6a48bf7dc78542d6bc2bc6a74fa9e2099e0bc"} {"question" "q-348730" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fd0fe482f3cf2728f94910c390bc6c5e148a5e519583c93f66dbd58dbdbd73"} {"question" "q-348730" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi^3}{96}+3\\pi"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fd0fe482f3cf2728f94910c390bc6c5e148a5e519583c93f66dbd58dbdbd73"} {"question" "q-348733" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/assets/b9a4695c6e43ee5ceb15ea1bbb3ee1815fdbd87e9c8b4a4e8eeba1089750ff79.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+3x+17,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=0,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fd0fe482f3cf2728f94910c390bc6c5e148a5e519583c93f66dbd58dbdbd73"} {"question" "q-348733" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+3x+17)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo calculate this integral, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rewrite the above formula as\n\n$$\n6\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x=6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+3x+17)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+3x+17)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+17x)\\,{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{0} \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+\\frac{3}{2}(0)^{2}+17\\cdot 0]-[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\pi )+\\frac{3}{2}{(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}+17(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =[0+0+0]-[0+\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{8}-\\frac{17\\pi }{2}] \\\\  & =[0+\\frac{17\\pi }{2}-\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{8}]-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pi }{2}-\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fd0fe482f3cf2728f94910c390bc6c5e148a5e519583c93f66dbd58dbdbd73"} {"question" "q-348733" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96b3c950dde71577c2afac8d52c6a48bf7dc78542d6bc2bc6a74fa9e2099e0bc"} {"question" "q-348733" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fd0fe482f3cf2728f94910c390bc6c5e148a5e519583c93f66dbd58dbdbd73"} {"question" "q-348733" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{17\\pi}{2}-\\frac{3\\pi^2}{8}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fd0fe482f3cf2728f94910c390bc6c5e148a5e519583c93f66dbd58dbdbd73"} {"question" "q-348735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }6{cos}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fd0fe482f3cf2728f94910c390bc6c5e148a5e519583c93f66dbd58dbdbd73"} {"question" "q-348735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $3,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n6{cos}^{2}⁡x=3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }6{cos}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+3x)|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )+3\\pi ]-[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}] \\\\  & =3\\pi -\\frac{3\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fd0fe482f3cf2728f94910c390bc6c5e148a5e519583c93f66dbd58dbdbd73"} {"question" "q-348735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96b3c950dde71577c2afac8d52c6a48bf7dc78542d6bc2bc6a74fa9e2099e0bc"} {"question" "q-348735" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fd0fe482f3cf2728f94910c390bc6c5e148a5e519583c93f66dbd58dbdbd73"} {"question" "q-348735" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "12fd0fe482f3cf2728f94910c390bc6c5e148a5e519583c93